From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:57:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU core idle states

Without idle states every idle A733 core stays in WFI with its power on.

Add one core power-down state per core type: PSCI power_state
0x00010000, which also stops the core's local timer. The latencies are
the worst case measured at the lowest operating point; the A76 wakes
more slowly than the A55. min-residency-us is the vendor's 3570 for
both: with 1000 the menu governor powers a core down between I/O
commands about 1 ms apart, most of those idles end early, and eMMC
reads of 256 KiB at queue depth 1 lose 5 % IOPS. 3570 keeps such gaps
in WFI and made no measurable difference to the idle power of the
board.

The state needs PSCI firmware that implements CPU_SUSPEND at the core
level.

Not covered: a cluster (DSU) power-down state.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; cpu-sleep-a55 and
cpu-sleep-a76 appear with 200 and 260 us latency, and all eight cores
enter them while idle. A few entries a minute return at once on a
pending interrupt.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index e54db89cfb32..5e8a4c127bb7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			reg = <0x000>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -74,6 +75,7 @@ cpu1: cpu@100 {
 			reg = <0x100>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -89,6 +91,7 @@ cpu2: cpu@200 {
 			reg = <0x200>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -104,6 +107,7 @@ cpu3: cpu@300 {
 			reg = <0x300>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -119,6 +123,7 @@ cpu4: cpu@400 {
 			reg = <0x400>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -134,6 +139,7 @@ cpu5: cpu@500 {
 			reg = <0x500>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -149,6 +155,7 @@ cpu6: cpu@600 {
 			reg = <0x600>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a76>;
 			i-cache-size = <65536>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <256>;
@@ -164,6 +171,7 @@ cpu7: cpu@700 {
 			reg = <0x700>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a76>;
 			i-cache-size = <65536>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <256>;
@@ -173,6 +181,28 @@ cpu7: cpu@700 {
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache7>;
 		};
 
+		idle-states {
+			entry-method = "psci";
+
+			cpu_sleep_a55: cpu-sleep-a55 {
+				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00010000>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+				entry-latency-us = <50>;
+				exit-latency-us = <150>;
+				min-residency-us = <3570>;
+			};
+
+			cpu_sleep_a76: cpu-sleep-a76 {
+				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00010000>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+				entry-latency-us = <50>;
+				exit-latency-us = <210>;
+				min-residency-us = <3570>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		l2_cache0: l2-cache-0 {
 			compatible = "cache";
 			cache-level = <2>;
